d\\\", the node's computed opacity stays 1 with no filter, and all 5 connected edges keep opacity 1 with unchanged classNames. The only observable effect was Coverage moving from 71% to 73%, suggesting some backend recalculation occurred, but there is no visible gray-out/hide indication on the node or edges as required.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-6\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Template Library section lists templates organized by job type/category (Software Engineer/Engineering, Product Manager/Product, HR Manager/Human Resources, Data Scientist/Analytics, Sales Manager/Sales) with preview info (competency count, connection count, tags) visible without opening each model.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-7\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Applying a template does not actually load its graph into the editor\", \"actual\": \"Clicking \\\"Apply\\\" on the \\\"Software Engineer\\\" template changed the page header title to \\\"Software Engineer\\\" and updated the Critical Path stat text to reference Software Engineer competency names (\\\"Programming Languages\\\", \\\"Problem Solving\\\", \\\"System Design\\\"), but the actual graph nodes remained the old HR Manager nodes (data-id: talent-acq, hr-compliance, perf-mgmt, emp-relations, leadership, org-dev) with their original names/edges unchanged. The model data is inconsistent/partially applied.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-8\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"No naming/description dialog when saving custom template; no \\\"My Templates\\\" retrieval area\", \"actual\": \"Clicking \\\"Save Current\\\" immediately shows a \\\"Template Saved\\\" toast with no dialog prompting for a template name or description (0 dialog elements in DOM). The Template Library list still shows only the same 5 original templates, with the current job's template card marked \\\"Current\\\" — no new distinct custom template entry was created, and there is no \\\"My Templates\\\" section to retrieve saved custom templates from.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-9\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Three scenario tabs (Recruitment, Training, Promotion) are switchable and each shows distinct content: \\\"Training Simulation\\\" panel with different default Level/Weight Change values (e.g. technical +1) vs \\\"Promotion Simulation\\\" panel (e.g. technical Weight Change -5%, behavioral +10%).\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-10\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Clicking \\\"Run Simulation\\\" in the Promotion scenario tab (with category weight adjustments -5%/+10%) changed the Critical Path indicator from \\\"3 competencies\\\" (Problem Solving, Programming Languages, System Design) to \\\"4 competencies\\\" (Problem Solving, Programming Languages, Collaboration, +1), demonstrating quantitative impact of the scenario adjustment on key model indicators.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-13\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Coverage % updated live after structural changes: 71%→74% after raising Talent Acquisition's level, then →64% after lowering HR Compliance's level, updating instantly with each interaction.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-15\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Details page renders a React Flow directed graph: nodes are competencies (Talent Acquisition, HR Compliance, Performance Management, Employee Relations, Leadership, Organizational Development) each showing level/weight/domain, and labeled edges (e.g. \\\"Edge from talent-acq to perf-mgmt\\\" 70%) representing weighted dependencies. Graph supports zoom in/out, fit view, minimap, toggle interactivity.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-16\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Critical path nodes are visually marked with \\\"border-node-critical\\\" class. After reducing Talent Acquisition's weight to minimum (0%) via its slider, critical path list updated in real time from [\\\"Talent Acquisition\\\",\\\"Employee Relations\\\",\\\"HR Compliance\\\"] to [\\\"Employee Relations\\\",\\\"HR Compliance\\\",\\\"Performance Management\\\"], showing live recalculation.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-17\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Lowering HR Compliance's level to minimum caused Risk Gaps to update from \\\"0 identified\\\" to \\\"1 identified\\\", listing \\\"HR Compliance\\\" as the risk gap.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-18\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"An alert banner \\\"Competency Gap Alert\\\" appeared prominently below the stats panel: \\\"1 competency below recommended level: HR Compliance. Consider increasing training focus or adjusting expectations.\\\"\"}]}"
      }
    ]
  }
